/ActualText (JUST LIKE ANY PROGRAMMING LANGUAGE, BEGINNERS OFTEN START WITH A SIMPLE "HELLO WORLD" PROGRAM TO GET A FEEL FOR THE SYNTAX AND STRUCTURE. IN THIS SECTION, READERS WILL LEARN HOW TO WRITE THEIR FIRST ARDUINO PROGRAM, WHICH TYPICALLY BLINKS AN LED CONNECTED TO ONE OF THE DIGITAL PINS ON THE BOARD. THEY'LL UNDERSTAND THE BASIC STRUCTURE OF AN ARDUINO SKETCH, HOW TO UPLOAD IT TO THE BOARD, AND HOW TO TROUBLESHOOT COMMON ERRORS.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
