317 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (FUNCTIONS ARE REUSABLE BLOCKS OF CODE THAT PERFORM A SPECIFIC TASK. THEY HELP ORGANIZE CODE INTO MANAGEABLE PIECES AND PROMOTE CODE REUSE. IN ARDUINO PROGRAMMING, FUNCTIONS HAVE A RETURN TYPE, A NAME, AND ZERO OR MORE PARAMETERS. YOU CAN DEFINE YOUR OWN FUNCTIONS OR USE BUILT-IN FUNCTIONS PROVIDED BY ARDUINO LIBRARIES.)
/E (FUNCTIONS ARE REUSABLE BLOCKS OF CODE THAT PERFORM A SPECIFIC TASK. THEY HELP ORGANIZE CODE INTO MANAGEABLE PIECES AND PROMOTE CODE REUSE. IN ARDUINO PROGRAMMING, FUNCTIONS HAVE A RETURN TYPE, A NAME, AND ZERO OR MORE PARAMETERS. YOU CAN DEFINE YOUR OWN FUNCTIONS OR USE BUILT-IN FUNCTIONS PROVIDED BY ARDUINO LIBRARIES.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
