326 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (ARDUINO BOARDS ARE EQUIPPED WITH BOTH DIGITAL AND ANALOG PINS, ALLOWING US TO INTERFACE WITH A WIDE VARIETY OF SENSORS. DIGITAL SENSORS OUTPUT BINARY SIGNALS \(0 OR 1\), WHILE ANALOG SENSORS PROVIDE CONTINUOUS VOLTAGE OR CURRENT OUTPUTS. COMMON DIGITAL SENSORS INCLUDE PUSH BUTTONS, MOTION DETECTORS, AND DIGITAL TEMPERATURE SENSORS, WHILE ANALOG SENSORS INCLUDE LIGHT SENSORS, TEMPERATURE SENSORS, AND POTENTIOMETERS.)
/E (ARDUINO BOARDS ARE EQUIPPED WITH BOTH DIGITAL AND ANALOG PINS, ALLOWING US TO INTERFACE WITH A WIDE VARIETY OF SENSORS. DIGITAL SENSORS OUTPUT BINARY SIGNALS \(0 OR 1\), WHILE ANALOG SENSORS PROVIDE CONTINUOUS VOLTAGE OR CURRENT OUTPUTS. COMMON DIGITAL SENSORS INCLUDE PUSH BUTTONS, MOTION DETECTORS, AND DIGITAL TEMPERATURE SENSORS, WHILE ANALOG SENSORS INCLUDE LIGHT SENSORS, TEMPERATURE SENSORS, AND POTENTIOMETERS.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
