/E (SERIAL COMMUNICATION IS A COMMON METHOD USED FOR TRANSMITTING DATA BETWEEN DEVICES OVER A SINGLE WIRE OR PAIR OF WIRES. ARDUINO BOARDS ARE EQUIPPED WITH HARDWARE UART \(UNIVERSAL ASYNCHRONOUS RECEIVER-TRANSMITTER\) MODULES THAT FACILITATE SERIAL COMMUNICATION VIA THE RX \(RECEIVE\) AND TX \(TRANSMIT\) PINS.)
