/T (SPI IS A SYNCHRONOUS SERIAL COMMUNICATION PROTOCOL COMMONLY USED FOR COMMUNICATION BETWEEN MICROCONTROLLERS AND PERIPHERAL DEVICES SUCH AS SENSORS, DISPLAYS, AND SD CARDS. IT USES FOUR COMMUNICATION LINES: MISO \(MASTER IN SLAVE OUT\), MOSI \(MASTER OUT SLAVE IN\), SCK \(SERIAL CLOCK\), AND SS \(SLAVE SELECT\).)
/E (SPI IS A SYNCHRONOUS SERIAL COMMUNICATION PROTOCOL COMMONLY USED FOR COMMUNICATION BETWEEN MICROCONTROLLERS AND PERIPHERAL DEVICES SUCH AS SENSORS, DISPLAYS, AND SD CARDS. IT USES FOUR COMMUNICATION LINES: MISO \(MASTER IN SLAVE OUT\), MOSI \(MASTER OUT SLAVE IN\), SCK \(SERIAL CLOCK\), AND SS \(SLAVE SELECT\).)
