>>
endobj
374 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (INTERRUPTS ARE A MECHANISM USED TO TEMPORARILY HALT THE NORMAL EXECUTION OF A PROGRAM TO HANDLE A SPECIFIC EVENT OR CONDITION. ARDUINO BOARDS SUPPORT VARIOUS TYPES OF INTERRUPTS, INCLUDING EXTERNAL INTERRUPTS TRIGGERED BY CHANGES ON DIGITAL PINS, TIMER INTERRUPTS TRIGGERED BY THE INTERNAL TIMERS, AND PIN CHANGE INTERRUPTS TRIGGERED BY CHANGES ON MULTIPLE PINS.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
