/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (PWM IS A TECHNIQUE USED TO GENERATE ANALOG-LIKE SIGNALS USING DIGITAL PINS. BY RAPIDLY SWITCHING A DIGITAL SIGNAL ON AND OFF AT VARYING DUTY CYCLES, PWM CAN SIMULATE AN ANALOG VOLTAGE OR CONTROL THE SPEED OF MOTORS AND THE BRIGHTNESS OF LEDS.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
